```suggestion
	if (p_enable == in_3d_space) {
		return;
	}
	in_3d_space = p_enable;
```
Same check as in most of the other setters to prevent regenerating the texture when the value is unchanged.

```suggestion
	Vector<uint8_t> data;
	data.resize(width * height * 4);

	uint8_t *wd8 = data.ptrw();

	for (int row = 0, x = 0; row < height; row++) {
		for (int col = 0; col < width; col++, x++) {
			Color pixel_color = p_image->get_pixel(col, row);
			Color ramp_color = color_ramp->get_color_at_offset(pixel_color.get_luminance());
			wd8[x * 4 + 0] = uint8_t(CLAMP(ramp_color.r * 255, 0, 255));
			wd8[x * 4 + 1] = uint8_t(CLAMP(ramp_color.g * 255, 0, 255));
			wd8[x * 4 + 2] = uint8_t(CLAMP(ramp_color.b * 255, 0, 255));
			wd8[x * 4 + 3] = uint8_t(CLAMP(ramp_color.a * 255, 0, 255));
		}
	}

	new_image->create(width, height, false, Image::FORMAT_RGBA8, data);
```

This is derived from the `FastNoiseLite::get_image()` function that was removed. It should be more performant than using `Image.set_pixel()` directly. I haven't tested this code, but it should work (or at least be close to working).
